// Craft families — the power-dice "how you solved it" catalog, and the twin
// expansion that turns each family into its Daily and Challenge collectibles.
//
// Extracted from ./badgeRegistry 2026-08-02: the registry had reached the
// 800-line structural cap, and this is the block that grows every time a feat is
// added. Pure metadata — no detection logic (that is src/equation-engine/ for
// the predicates and src/stats-aggregation/craftStages.js for the rungs), no
// React, no I/O.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE 2026-09-03 MERGE — 17 feats became 8 families
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Design: .crispy/sessions/2026-08-24-badges-overhaul/design-per-mode-2026-08-31.md
// § 2, ruled by David 2026-08-31 on the evidence of
// craft-overlap-audit-2026-08-31.md.
//
// The audit found 10 craft feats and 7 perfect variants built from NINE
// predicates, with **nine subsumption pairs** — pairs where one card can never
// light without the other lighting too:
//
//   bigBang          ⊃ fullSpectrum   (usesAllFourOpsWithExponent ⊃ usesAllFourOps)
//   lightningDivide  ⊃ greatDivide    (the same feat, plus a sub-60s clause)
//   …and the seven perfect variants, each ⊃ the base feat it shadowed.
//
// A subsumption pair is not two achievements. It is ONE achievement that pops
// twice, wearing two unrelated names — a player could not tell that Fission and
// The Great Divide were the same thing. David's ruling: collapse each pair into
// an extra RUNG of the surviving family, so the prestige is a higher tier of a
// badge you already hold rather than a second card beside it.
//
// So `bigBang` is now Full Spectrum's "Big Bang" rung, `supernova` its
// "Supernova" rung, `fission` The Great Divide's top rung, and so on. Each rung
// KEEPS the retired badge's name and its art (`tierIcons` below), because the
// name is what the player earned — only the card it hangs on changed.
//
// MIGRATION COST: ZERO, verified. There is no server-side badge table; badge
// state is DERIVED from `daily_challenge_times` and `practice_solves` on every
// read (design § 1). Retiring an id costs nobody anything — it recomputes as a
// higher tier of the survivor. The only persistence is the per-device
// `announcedBadges` snapshot, which is why every merged entry carries
// `availableFrom: CRAFT_MERGE_DATE`: it routes a first earn discovered from
// pre-merge history into the ONE retroactive summary rather than a queue of pops
// (`retroactiveCutoff` in src/game-flow/badgeAnnouncements.js).
//
// ⚠️ NO RUNG MAY DEMOTE A HOLDER. Design § 1's promise is "nobody loses it", so
// each merged ladder KEEPS every count rung its pre-merge badge had — Full
// Spectrum still has ×10/×37/×100, The Great Divide still has ×100 — even where
// the design table listed only the new qualitative rungs. A player sitting on
// tier 3 of the old countLadder lands at or above tier 3 of the new stage
// ladder, never below. `craftFeats.test.js` pins that mapping feat by feat.
//
// STILL OUT OF SCOPE (step 2, the per-mode extension): the Easy On-Ramp badges
// that share these predicates — `tower`, `everyWhichWay`, `deepNest`,
// `bracketRookie`, `roundTrip` — are NOT absorbed here. Absorbing one means
// giving its family an Easy cell, which is exactly the per-mode extension the
// design defers to a later slice. They stay in ./onRampBadges, untouched.

import { stageLadder } from './badgeScaling';

/**
 * Re-declared locally as JSDoc aliases because these shapes are DEFINED in
 * ./badgeRegistry, which imports this module at runtime. A type-only reference
 * back is safe (tsc resolves it; madge sees only a comment, so no dependency
 * cycle is introduced) and keeps the annotations below readable.
 *
 * @typedef {import('./badgeRegistry').BadgeDefinition} BadgeDefinition
 * @typedef {import('./badgeRegistry').BadgeMode} BadgeMode
 * @typedef {import('./badgeRegistry').BadgeCategory} BadgeCategory
 */

/**
 * The date the merged families entered the catalog. Every entry below carries it
 * as `availableFrom`, so `retroactiveCutoff` folds the whole re-cut into a single
 * summary moment instead of a storm of pops for solves made months ago.
 */
export const CRAFT_MERGE_DATE = '2026-09-03';

/**
 * The date the per-tier entries (Easy Daily, Expert Daily, Expert practice)
 * entered the catalog. Badges are DERIVED from history, so an Expert player's
 * past solves light these the moment they ship — and that must arrive as ONE
 * retroactive summary, not a queue of pops for solves made weeks ago.
 * `retroactiveCutoff` in src/game-flow/badgeAnnouncements.js reads it.
 */
export const THREE_MODE_BADGES_DATE = '2026-09-04';

/**
 * How an Expert craft badge ladders. Once every solve is perfect, the only axis
 * with anything left to say is how OFTEN — so the perfect feat is rung 1 and
 * repetition is the climb.
 */
const EXPERT_REPEATS = [
  { suffix: '', times: 1, label: (name) => name },
  { suffix: 'X10', times: 10, label: (name) => `${name} ×10` },
  { suffix: 'X37', times: 37, label: (name) => `${name} ×37` },
];

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CRAFT — eight families, each one badge with a deep ladder.
//
// Every family is earnable on the Daily AND in Challenge free-play, and the two
// are SEPARATE collectibles (David, 2026-07-30): the Daily wears the
// aspirational marquee name and gets the prestige frame; Challenge wears the
// humbler practice/training name. Same detection, two entries.
//
// `how`     — the whole-badge sentence (becomes `criteriaText`). It describes the
//             CLIMB, because a merged family's rungs are different questions and
//             one requirement sentence can no longer cover them all.
// `stages`  — the rungs, low → high. `key` is the detection key, whose predicate
//             lives in src/stats-aggregation/craftStages.js; `label` is the rung
//             name the card caption and the detail carousel render.
// `absorbs` — the featIds this family retired into rungs. Documentation, and the
//             pin `badgeRegistry.test.js` reads to assert none ever comes back.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

