// Pure timing policy for the rocket-launch loading mask (daily-win celebration).
//
// On a daily win the rocket overlays the results screen while SuccessModal
// computes its "what was possible" solver UNDERNEATH; when the rocket finishes
// flying it lifts away to reveal the already-loaded results. This module owns the
// "how long does the rocket fly" decision so the policy is testable without
// React / DOM / timers.
//
// Policy (David's 2026-07-12 interview — "latency mask, min ~1.2s, cap ~4s"):
//   - MIN floor: always fly at least MIN_MS so the launch feels intentional, even
//     if the results are ready instantly. Never adds delay beyond this floor.
//   - READY handoff: once the results signal ready AND the floor has passed, hand
//     off immediately — don't hold the user for the full cap.
//   - CAP ceiling: never trap the user past CAP_MS, even if "ready" never fires
//     (a slow solver must not strand them on the rocket).

// The rocket is the marquee daily-win moment (once per day) — it's tuned to be
// SEEN in full, not to be the shortest possible mask. MIN guarantees the whole
// ~2.0s flight plays even when results are ready instantly (the floor must not be
// cut short by a fast load); CAP still bounds a genuinely slow solver. Keep MIN ≈
// the flight duration in RocketLaunchScreen so the rocket is animating the entire
// time. Tuned down from 3.2s/5.5s (David 2026-07-26, L2-3): the earlier floor
// felt too long on Daily/Easy — 2.0s still lets the arc complete without waiting.
export const ROCKET_MIN_MS = 2000;
export const ROCKET_CAP_MS = 4000;

/**
 * Decide whether the rocket should hand off to the results yet.
 *
 * @param {{ elapsedMs: number, ready?: boolean, minMs?: number, capMs?: number }} args
 *   elapsedMs — ms since the rocket launched (negative is clamped to 0).
 *   ready — have the background results finished loading?
 *   minMs / capMs — floor and ceiling (defaults ROCKET_MIN_MS / ROCKET_CAP_MS).
 * @returns {{ done: boolean, remainingMs: number }}
 *   done — the rocket should dismiss now.
 *   remainingMs — ms until the next possible handoff given current knowledge
 *     (0 when done; time to the floor when still below it; else time to the cap).
 */
export function computeRocketHandoff({ elapsedMs, ready = false, minMs = ROCKET_MIN_MS, capMs = ROCKET_CAP_MS }) {
  const e = Math.max(0, elapsedMs || 0);
  // Cap is the hard ceiling and wins even if it sits below the floor.
  if (e >= capMs) return { done: true, remainingMs: 0 };
  // Floor holds regardless of ready — the launch must feel intentional.
  if (e < minMs) return { done: false, remainingMs: minMs - e };
  // Floor passed: hand off the instant results are ready, else wait for the cap.
  if (ready) return { done: true, remainingMs: 0 };
  return { done: false, remainingMs: capMs - e };
}

/**
 * The total flight duration given when (if ever) the results become ready.
 * Handy for scheduling a single dismiss timer instead of polling.
 *
 * @param {{ readyAtMs?: number|null, minMs?: number, capMs?: number }} args
 *   readyAtMs — ms after launch that results became ready (null = never / unknown).
 * @returns {number} clamp(readyAtMs, minMs, capMs); capMs when never ready.
 */
export function rocketFlightDurationMs({ readyAtMs = null, minMs = ROCKET_MIN_MS, capMs = ROCKET_CAP_MS }) {
  if (readyAtMs == null) return capMs;
  return Math.min(capMs, Math.max(minMs, readyAtMs));
}
