// How long a Daily attempt lasts — the number, the clock label, and nothing else.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHY THIS IS ONE MODULE AND NOT A CONSTANT PER CALLER
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The limit was ONE HOUR until 2026-09-12 (David: "instead of getting an hour,
// contestants will now get 15:37"). Before this module it was written down in
// four independent places — `ONE_HOUR_MS` in the attempt hook, a separate
// `DAILY_LIMIT_SECONDS` beside it, `ONE_HOUR_MS` again in staleDailyNotice, and
// the words "up to 1 hour" hand-typed into the rules modal and the failure
// explainer.
//
// Four copies of one rule is four chances for the clock and the copy to disagree,
// and a rules screen that misstates the limit is the specific failure that cost
// delaney-37 a 7h40m attempt (see ChallengeWarningModal). So the number and the
// words a player reads both come from here, and the label is DERIVED from the
// number rather than typed beside it.
//
// ⚠️ THE SERVER HAS ITS OWN COPY AND IT IS DELIBERATELY STILL 3600.
// `supabase/functions/_shared/dailySolveGate.ts` carries `WINDOW_SECONDS`, which
// `submit-daily-time` enforces against the authoritative `attempt.created_at`.
// It was NOT changed alongside this, on purpose:
//
//   Every player on production OTA 1.0.306 or store build 1.0.291 believes they
//   have an hour. Tightening the server before they update would reject their
//   solve as `expired` the moment they passed 15:37 — silently losing the daily
//   for someone playing in good faith, which is exactly the failure this app has
//   already inflicted once.
//
// The server window is a CHEAT CEILING, not the rule. Leaving it loose while the
// client enforces the real limit costs nothing: the client stops the player at
// 937s, so the server never sees a later submit from an updated build.
//
// Tighten it AFTER the production OTA carrying this reaches players — not after
// a beta, which reaches only manually-assigned test devices. Tracked at
// `.workshop/FOLLOWUP-daily-window-server.md`.

/** The attempt window, in seconds. 15:37 — on-brand with the target. */
export const DAILY_LIMIT_SECONDS = 15 * 60 + 37;

/** The same wall in milliseconds, for comparisons against a server timestamp. */
export const DAILY_LIMIT_MS = DAILY_LIMIT_SECONDS * 1000;

/**
 * The limit as a player reads it on a clock: `15:37`.
 *
 * DERIVED, not typed. A hand-written "15:37" beside a `937` is the drift this
 * module exists to prevent — change the number and this follows it.
 *
 * @returns {string}
 */
export const DAILY_LIMIT_LABEL = `${Math.floor(DAILY_LIMIT_SECONDS / 60)}:${String(DAILY_LIMIT_SECONDS % 60).padStart(2, '0')}`;
